Keep the centering style alive across cmd_merge_cells_redo.

sheet_apply_style absorbs a reference to the partial style it is given
(sheet.c: "@style: (transfer full)"; sheet_style_apply_range unrefs it), but
cmd_merge_cells_redo applied one align-center style to every merged range
and then unreffed it once more, so Merge and Center freed the style after
the first range and tripped "gnm_style_unref: assertion 'style->ref_count >
0' failed" (a use after free with several ranges).  Found through the Cocoa
front end on 2026-10-11; the GTK front end runs the same code.  Take a
reference per range so the final unref balances.

--- a/src/commands.c	2026-10-11 09:06:31
+++ b/src/commands.c	2026-10-11 09:06:31
@@ -4143,8 +4143,11 @@
 		g_slist_free (merged);
 
 		gnm_sheet_merge_add (sheet, r, TRUE, GO_CMD_CONTEXT (wbc));
-		if (me->center)
+		if (me->center) {
+			/* sheet_apply_style absorbs a reference */
+			gnm_style_ref (align_center);
 			sheet_apply_style (me->cmd.sheet, r, align_center);
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (me->center)
